  "body": "@igrigorik, could use some help here.\n\nCurrently the HTML spec only specifies prefetch. https://w3c.github.io/resource-hints/ has several others:\n- dns-prefetch\n- preconnect\n- prerender\n\nWhich of these have multi-vendor support? What is their implementation status?\n\nFor those that are broadly supported, I think it would be beneficial to add them to HTML, with a link to the Resource Hints spec for more information. This would allow authors to get a centralized idea of what are the link relations with normative impacts, in the link types table; it would also take care of currently-unspecified things like whether `relList.supports(\"preconnect\")` should work, whether they are body-ok, or whether they can appear on `<a>` and `<area>` elements or just on `<link>` elements.\n\nLet us know!\n",
